        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8805/3 Undifferentiated sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63847,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B5F.0 &amp; XH6HY6 Sarcoma, not elsewhere classified of uterus &amp; Undifferentiated sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63848,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63849,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63850,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Endometrium and/or myometrium and rarely cervix</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63851,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients are typically postmenopausal {25341584; 30789359; 28622181; 18580489} and present with abnormal uterine bleeding, pelvic pain/pressure, and symptoms related to extrauterine disease {30772825}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63852,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are rare {25341584; 21826194; 30541504}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63853,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63854,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours show activation of RNA expression pathways related to genital tract development, extracellular matrix, muscle function, and proliferation, as well as heterogeneous copy-number alterations. Some tumours show extensive chromosomal gains and losses; others are near diploid {30617134}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63855,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Undifferentiated uterine sarcomas form large intracavitary and polypoid or intramural fleshy masses with haemorrhage and necrosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63856,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Like its soft tissue counterpart, undifferentiated uterine sarcoma shows no identifiable line of differentiation. At present, this is considered likely to be a heterogeneous group of tumours and a diagnosis of exclusion. Therefore, adequate sampling is important.</p>\r\n<p>Undifferentiated uterine sarcomas typically display a destructive pattern of myometrial invasion. In the past these tumours have been classified as uniform and pleomorphic types {18580489}. In tumours with uniform nuclear features, <em>YWHAE</em>-<em>NUTM2</em>&nbsp;(<em>FAM22</em>) high-grade endometrial stromal sarcoma should be excluded. Some of these tumours are associated with a low-grade endometrial stromal component and diffusely express cyclin&nbsp;D1. However, others with pleomorphic histology are also associated with a low-grade component, and are designated high-grade endometrial stromal sarcoma NOS. Thus, currently, tumours within the category of undifferentiated uterine sarcoma typically consist of sheets of uniform or pleomorphic epithelioid and/or spindled cells associated with brisk mitotic activity. Necrosis and lymphovascular invasion are commonly seen {19898427}. Tumours are often positive for p53 and p16, and some may show positivity for ER and/or PR, as well as variable positivity for CD10 {15863163}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-24T16:23:11"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63857,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63858,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>YWHAE</em>, <em>JAZF1</em>, and NTRK rearrangements may underpin rare pleomorphic sarcomas that should not be classified in this category {28621321; 11371647; 29553955; 30877273}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63859,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> uniform or pleomorphic high-grade mesenchymal cells with brisk mitotic activity; exclusion of other high-grade tumours by extensive sampling (poorly differentiated carcinoma, carcinosarcoma, sarcomatous overgrowth in adenosarcoma) and immunohistochemistry for <em>ZC3H7B</em>-<em>BCOR</em>, <em>YWHAE</em>-<em>NUTM2</em> (<em>FAM22</em>), and <em>BCOR</em> ITD high-grade endometrial stromal sarcomas and NTRK sarcomas.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> exclusion of the presence of fusion genes associated with other sarcoma types may be required.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-24T16:23:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63860,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This entity is staged as uterine sarcoma using the FIGO, Union for International Cancer Control (UICC), or American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) system.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63861,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 247,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are associated with a poor prognosis; however, mitotic count and hormone receptor expression appear to define a group of cases in which long-term survival can be achieved {28622181; 30617134}. ER and/or PR expression is associated with improved overall survival {25130488; 30617134}. The expression of genes related to extracellular matrix and an elevated mitotic count, respectively, may correlate with decreased overall and 5-year survival {25130488; 30617134; 28622181}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-05T17:05:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]